<%# "Forgot your password?" — POSTs `user[email]` to Devise's password path, which
    mails the reset instructions. Devise is configured paranoid, so the response never
    reveals whether the address exists; the error summary below is therefore reachable
    only for a malformed submit.

    DESIGN SYSTEM (Slice 9, Task 4.6) — the shared auth treatment: `ui/_card` for the
    white SQUARE panel, the field-border token plus the indigo focus border in place of
    a bare uncoloured border resolving to body ink, the 14px muted label, and the
    `rect` solid submit the design system assigns to auth screens.
%>
<%= render layout: "ui/card", locals: {class: "max-w-md mx-auto mt-16 p-6"} do %>
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-6">Forgot your password?</h2>

  <%= form_for(resource, as: resource_name, url: password_path(resource_name), html: { method: :post }) do |f| %>
    <%= render "devise/shared/error_messages", resource: resource %>

    <div class="mb-3">
      <%= f.label :email, class: "block text-sm text-grey mb-1" %>
      <%= f.email_field :email, autofocus: true, autocomplete: "email",
            class: "w-full rounded border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 focus:outline-none focus:border-primary" %>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-4">
      <%= f.submit "Send me password reset instructions", class: ds_button_classes(variant: :rect) %>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <%= render "devise/shared/links" %>
<% end %>
